%description:

Tcp.fastopenMaxPendingRequests:limit -- connection A gets Fast Open, and connection B, with A pending, does not.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "TCP Fast Open, server: the largest number of Fast Open connections of a
listener in SYN_RCVD (PendingFastOpenRequests, RFC 7413 section 4.2 ...); above it, a SYN gets no
Fast Open: no cookie, and its data is not acknowledged".

The classes: ample (16, the default: more than the pending connections of the test), limit (a
value that the pending connections reach), zero (0: no Fast Open at all). The code:
TcpConnection::processSynInListen() gives a SYN no Fast Open when the Fast Open
connections of the listener in SYN_RCVD reach the value: no cookie, and the data of the SYN is
not acknowledged (RFC 7413 section 4.2). This test separates "limit" from the other values.

Host under test: host2, a Fast Open server; host1 is a Fast Open client (preconditions). host1
gets a cookie at 0.1 s; at 0.5 s it opens connection A with 500 bytes on the SYN, and the tap
drops each later segment of connection A, so that it stays in SYN_RCVD at host2; at 0.6 s host1
opens connection B with 500 bytes on the SYN. Observation: level 1, connection A gets Fast Open, and connection B, with A pending, does not.

%# parameter: Tcp.fastopenMaxPendingRequests
%# class: limit
%# value: 1
%# key: *.host2.tcp.fastopenMaxPendingRequests
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpFastopenMaxPendingRequestsLimit")
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 1 with Fast Open"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie == "";
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN of connection 1: a cookie request")
                  .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie.size() == 16;
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN-ACK of the first connection: a cookie")
                  .within(0.5))
        .act(action().at(0.5).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[1]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); app.sendData(app.socket(), 500); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 2 with Fast Open, and sends 500 bytes"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isnA", "tcp.sequenceNo").capture("portA", "tcp.srcPort")
             .describe("the SYN of connection A")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.srcPort == {portA} && tcp.synBit == false").drop()
                       .describe("each later segment of connection A: it stays in SYN_RCVD at host2"))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isnA} + 501")
             .describe("the SYN-ACK of connection A")
             .within(0.5))
        .act(action().at(0.6).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[2]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); app.sendData(app.socket(), 500); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 3 with Fast Open, and sends 500 bytes"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isnB", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of connection B")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isnB} + 1")
             .describe("the SYN-ACK of connection B")
             .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpFastopenMaxPendingRequestsLimit compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.fastopenMaxPendingRequests = 1    # the parameter under test
*.host2.tcp.fastopenServerEnabled = true
*.host1.tcp.fastopenClientEnabled = true
*.host1.numApps = 3
*.host1.app[*].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpFastopenMaxPendingRequestsLimit: PASS
